meta {
  name: List Run Rows (1-800 Review)
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/carrier-reconciliation/runs/{{reconRunId}}/rows?tab=review_1800&pageSize=25
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{reconToken}}
}

params:query {
  tab: review_1800
  pageSize: 25
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.getBody().items.length) {
    bru.setVar("reconRowId", res.getBody().items[0].id);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the 1-800 line, flagged by a Bind ID on no user", function () {
    const row = res.getBody().items.find((item) => item.dash.bindId === "OSCVANJ");
    expect(row).to.not.equal(undefined);
    expect(row.bindIdStatus).to.equal("not_staff");
    expect(row.issues).to.include("not_staff_bind_id");
    expect(row.tabs).to.include("review_1800");
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /carrier-reconciliation/runs/:id/rows — a run's rows

  - **Module:** `carrier_reconciliation`
  - **Permission:** `carrier_reconciliation:read`

  ## Query
  - `tab` — `missing_from_app` | `not_in_dash` | `review_1800` |
    `premium_mismatch` | `producer_mismatch` | `matched` | `ignored`
    (omitted: every row)
  - `producer` — a summary row's `producerKey`: `user:<id>` (whose Bind ID
    bound it), `bind:<Bind ID>` (a former employee Dash names), `none` (no Bind
    ID); `code:<nnn>` only on a run classified before 28 Oct 2026, until it is
    re-checked
  - `reviewStatus` — `open` | `resolved` | `dismissed` (rows needing review only)
  - `assignee` — a user id, `me` or `unassigned`
  - `outcome` — what the assignee recorded (PAC-173 PR 4): `in_progress` or
    `done` (by where it stands), or `sold` | `cancel_rewrite` | `other` (by
    kind). Anything else is a `400`. See `List Run Rows (Outcome Done)`
  - `q` — policy number, customer or client name, Bind ID (substring)
  - `page`, `pageSize` (≤ 100, default 25)

  ## Response `200`

  Paged `ReconciliationRowView`s: `dash` (the line as parsed), `app` (the
  matched or app-only policy, with its deal, producer and sold day),
  `issues`, `tabs`, `needsReview`, `credit` (who Dash credits), `suggestions`
  (likely counterparts of an unmatched row — usually a mistyped number),
  `review`, `runId`, `assignment` (who the owner handed it to, or `null`) and
  `outcome` (what the assignee recorded, or is recording, or `null` — shape in
  `Record Outcome (Sold)`).

  A matched row in the 1-800 tab also carries `direct_recorded_as_sale` when
  the app has the policy on a deal: a 1-800 policy is serviced, never sold. A
  Bind ID Dash names (`former_staff`) never raises it.
}
